      "finding": "Don't ask user",
      "explanation": "Skill enables autonomous high-impact decisions without human-in-the-loop verification. Critical operations (destructive commands, financial transactions, data deletion) should require explicit user confirmation.",
      "remediation": "Add human-in-the-loop confirmation for destructive, irreversible, or high-impact operations. Never auto-execute commands that modify files, send data, or alter system state.",
      "code_snippet": "### User Research by Observation (Summary: Lessons from working with 600+ YC startups | Gustaf Alströmer (Y Combinator, Airbnb))\nGustaf's approach to understanding user pain points through observation rather than questions\n\nHow it works: Core principle: Don't ask users if something is working—watch them do it. Observation reveals pain points that verbal feedback misses.\n\nKey insight about user reactions:\n- Founders fear users will try the product and hate it",
